---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const description =
  'The programs the OpenAR Collective is organized to run: open-source software, open knowledge, shared standards, training, and a neutral practitioner community, with the current status of each.';
---

<Base title="Programs" description={description}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="page-head">
      <p class="overline">Programs</p>
      <h1>What the Foundation is building</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Everything the Foundation builds and publishes will be free to use. Nothing it publishes
        will require membership, payment, or a commercial relationship of any kind.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="status-note" role="note">
      <h2>Where things stand</h2>
      <p>
        The Foundation was incorporated in April 2026 and seated its founding Board in July. Its
        work right now is telling the industry it exists and building the community that will shape
        everything else. The programs below describe what the Foundation is organized to do, not a
        catalogue of services running today. Each one carries its current status, and this page will
        be updated as programs launch.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="program" aria-labelledby="software">
      <h2 id="software">Open-source software <span class="tag">In design</span></h2>
      <p>
        The Foundation's flagship program will be a production-grade accounts receivable and
        collections platform that any organization can download, run, modify, and redistribute
        without a vendor relationship, a license fee, or permission from anyone. The software
        comprises two layers: the Wax application framework, a domain-agnostic foundation for
        auditable business applications, and the HiveAR accounts receivable platform built on it.
      </p>
      <p>
        The platform is in its initial architecture and design phase, and no source has been
        published yet. It will be released under the Apache License, Version 2.0, with source code
        published publicly on
        the <a href="https://github.com/OpenAR-Collective" rel="noopener">GitHub organization</a> and
        outside contributions accepted under the Developer Certificate of Origin. Compliance is a
        design principle rather than an add-on: tamper-evident audit trails, fine-grained access
        controls, and configurable compliance workflows are core architectural commitments.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Foundation is not a software vendor. It will steward the platform on behalf of the
        industry and the public, and it will never charge for it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="program" aria-labelledby="knowledge">
      <h2 id="knowledge">Open knowledge <span class="tag">Planned</span></h2>
      <p>
        The Foundation will publish open educational content, including guides, articles, white
        papers, and recorded webinars, addressing operational and compliance topics in accounts
        receivable. A library of plain-language compliance resources will cover the FDCPA, the FCRA,
        Regulation F, and key state-level consumer protection statutes, written to be accessible to
        practitioners who may lack dedicated legal or compliance staff.
      </p>
      <p class="notice">
        Compliance and regulatory resources published by the Foundation are educational reference
        materials only. They describe general regulatory frameworks and do not constitute legal
        advice, create an attorney-client relationship, or address the specific circumstances of any
        organization. Retain qualified legal counsel for guidance specific to your operations.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="program" aria-labelledby="standards">
      <h2 id="standards">Shared standards <span class="tag">Planned</span></h2>
      <p>
        The Foundation will develop shared technical and operational standards for the industry,
        including integration standards and published naming conventions for community
        contributions. Standards will be developed in the open, with community input, and published
        freely so any vendor or agency can implement them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="program" aria-labelledby="training">
      <h2 id="training">Training <span class="tag">Planned</span></h2>
      <p>
        The Foundation will deliver training through free webinars and virtual workshops open to the
        entire community, with recordings archived for asynchronous viewing. As the platform
        matures, a formal certification and training program will follow for the vendors and
        professionals who work with it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Certification examinations, courses, and renewals may carry fees, which support the
        Foundation's programs. Fees and standards will be uniform across applicants, and no
        applicant will receive preferential treatment based on a relationship to the Foundation, its
        leadership, or its directors. Certification will never gate the software: the platform is
        open source, and anyone may run, modify, and build on it without certification of any kind.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="program" aria-labelledby="community">
      <h2 id="community">Neutral community <span class="tag tag-live">Open now</span></h2>
      <p>
        The Foundation maintains a peer community, hosted on Discord, that is open to every
        practitioner in the industry: compliance officers, developers, operations managers,
        collectors, agency owners, attorneys, consumer advocates, academics, and regulators.
        Commercial solicitation is prohibited, there are no sponsored channels, and no one can buy
        visibility.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is where the Foundation's work starts. The community is the incubator from which the
        other programs emerge, and the direction those programs take will be set by the
        practitioners who participate. Joining now means helping decide what gets built first.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/join">Join the community</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .status-note {
    border: 1px solid var(--c-line);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--c-amber);
    border-radius: 3px;
    background: rgba(22, 20, 16, 0.5);
    padding: 1.35rem 1.6rem 1.5rem;
  }

  .status-note h2 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }

  .status-note p {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    color: var(--c-text-soft);
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }

  .program {
    margin-top: 2.75rem;
  }

  .program h2 {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  /* Status of each program, so the page never reads as a menu of things that
     are already running. */
  .tag {
    font-family: var(--f-sans);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--c-muted);
    border: 1px solid var(--c-line);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.7rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .tag-live {
    color: var(--c-amber);
    border-color: rgba(232, 160, 32, 0.45);
  }

  .program p {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--c-text-soft);
  }

  .notice {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
</style>
